  "answer": "Yes. Under Clause 29A of the CPWD General Conditions of Contract, any sum due to the contractor may be withheld or retained by the Engineer‑in‑Charge as a lien against any claim arising out of or under any other contract the contractor has with the Engineer‑in‑Charge or the Government (S1). Clause 29 similarly authorises the Engineer‑in‑Charge or Government to withhold and retain sums from the present contract to satisfy a claim arising from another contract (S7). However, the contractor has no right to claim interest (or any damages) on the amount that is withheld or retained, as expressly stated in Clause 29A and reiterated in Clause 29 (S1, S8)."
}

